WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.842
Fatigue is a performance constraint.

00:00:01.842 --> 00:00:04.977
It can reduce attention, slow reactions, weaken working memory,

00:00:04.977 --> 00:00:07.068
and make error detection less reliable.

00:00:07.068 --> 00:00:10.900
In technical work, that might mean missing a subtle configuration problem.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.687
In operations, it might mean skipping a check.

00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:14.384
In writing,

00:00:14.384 --> 00:00:19.261
it might mean failing to notice that the argument no longer supports the conclusion.

00:00:19.261 --> 00:00:22.048
Fatigue can also affect emotional regulation and confidence.

00:00:22.048 --> 00:00:26.926
People may become more reactive, more impatient, or more certain than the evidence supports.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:32.152
Overconfidence under fatigue is especially risky because the person may not realize performance has degraded.

00:00:32.152 --> 00:00:36.332
They may continue making decisions with the same level of confidence while

00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:38.074
using weaker attention and judgment.

00:00:38.074 --> 00:00:41.210
Performance risk matters in driving, safety-sensitive roles, incident response,

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:45.042
medical and operational settings, and any work where errors can compound.

00:00:45.042 --> 00:00:48.526
This course does not provide safety policy or medical guidance,

00:00:48.526 --> 00:00:52.706
but it does emphasize that recovery is part of responsible performance design.

00:00:52.706 --> 00:00:56.190
Teams should recognize when performance problems may be recovery problems.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.674
Persistent sleep, health, or safety concerns belong with qualified help.

00:00:59.674 --> 00:01:04.552
In learning and workplace design, the practical response is to treat fatigue as information.

00:01:04.552 --> 00:01:08.384
Adjust the task, add review, slow down when stakes are high,

00:01:08.384 --> 00:01:11.171
rotate roles when possible, or reschedule demanding work.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:15.700
Trying harder is not always the right answer when the system is under-recovered.
